{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An external push can stale an approval without making the PR a digest candidate, causing a needed review to be missed."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"A running change round can be reported as awaiting review, prompting review work on a head that is being replaced."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A confirmed merge recorded only on the run can be reported as needing review or having unknown PR state, prompting unnecessary action."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A historical blocked land takes precedence over a closed PR and directs an agent to retry an operation that will be refused."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Harmless text requiring exactly five decoding rounds blocks publication even with an empty denylist."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable privacy policy causes successful mutations to lose their confirmation and identifiers, risking duplicate work on retry."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A short registered credential can withhold ordinary response keys and values, making tool results unusable."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable privacy policy removes the status tool's state and next action, leaving the agent without its guidance."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Sequential reads can add session-start latency for a large unread feed, but the evidence establishes no timeout or lost work."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A fresh approval without a saved PR snapshot is counted as awaiting review, potentially causing redundant review work."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unknown run filter returns a structured 400 response rather than 404, an API consistency issue without a demonstrated runtime failure."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"MCP approvals are persisted and reported as human approvals, creating a misleading audit trail that can affect later decisions."},{"id":"C13","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An exceptionally long input can produce a very long digest line, though the specified line-count limit is preserved."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The same status defect as C8 omits state and next-action guidance when the privacy policy is unreadable."}]}